.TH IO_DESTROY 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
io_destroy \- destroys a kernel asynchronous i/o context, waiting for outstanding requests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/aio.h>
.B int io_destroy(aio_context_t context);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Destroys a kernel asynchronous I/O context, waiting for outstanding requests. This is the Linux kernel AIO ABI, not POSIX aio.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR io_destroy (2)
